Agent Checkpoint Strategy

Status: Accepted

Context:
- Agents may be killed or crash due to VRAM allocation challenges before finishing a Step.

Decision:
- When an agent is nearing its maximum VRAM allocation, a two tiered strategy will be implemented.
  - First, attempt to purge old cache history to free up memory.
  - If that fails to free up memory, force the agent to generate a checkpoint.json file
    to secure continuous processing by a new agent.

Consequences:
- Prevents VRAM issues like swaps

